{"base_rate":0.3989431968295905,"brier":0.17465099075297227,"bss":0.27164270722654826,"bss_hi":0.36420484986133017,"bss_lo":0.16240101284492547,"chart":{"base":[406.9,171.3],"fp":[375.4,202.0],"lead":"62,257.5 272,243.5 482,206.9 692,146.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.27 — higher than 42% of cities","fp":"low end +10pp, high end +18pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 60% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 13%; promised 100% → rained 83%"},"rel":"70.1,409.1 216.1,352.3 539,200.6 690.5,108.8"},"country":"SE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.11421400264200789,"ess":473.50912919772276,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Stockholm</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Stockholm rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>83%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>11%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nSTOCKHOLM_A, 1.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.27, ranked 126 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(71&ndash;161) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>204</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>17%</b></td><td class='num'>92</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'><b>33%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>62%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>90%</td><td class='num'><b>75%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>83%</b></td><td class='num'>156</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Stockholm</b> <span class=\"muted\">Sweden</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;40% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 40% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.27</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>71&ndash;161\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Stockholm &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Stockholm\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.1214705882353,380.2156862745098 72.42934782608695,350.3478260869565 115.0077922077922,292.1818181818182 175.0088,221.84 278.02461538461534,116.0 375.9863999999999,32.56 411.1376923076923,18.0 411.1376923076923,22.66666666666663 375.9863999999999,81.09333333333336 278.02461538461534,195.33333333333334 175.0088,299.49333333333334 115.0077922077922,348.9090909090909 72.42934782608695,378.04347826086956 58.1214705882353,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"236.78467635402905\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"236.78467635402905\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.1214705882353,340.96078431372547 72.42934782608695,318.69565217391306 115.0077922077922,311.0909090909091 175.0088,260.6666666666667 278.02461538461534,204.66666666666666 375.9863999999999,110.21333333333331 411.1376923076923,81.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 11% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 204 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.1214705882353\" cy=\"340.96078431372547\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 17% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 92 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"72.42934782608695\" cy=\"318.69565217391306\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 16%&amp;#10;It rained 19% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"115.0077922077922\" cy=\"311.0909090909091\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 33%&amp;#10;It rained 33% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"175.0088\" cy=\"260.6666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 62%&amp;#10;It rained 49% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"278.02461538461534\" cy=\"204.66666666666666\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 90%&amp;#10;It rained 75% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"375.9863999999999\" cy=\"110.21333333333331\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 83% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 156 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.1376923076923\" cy=\"81.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(40%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Stockholm the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.50) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.04).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'>-0.036</td><td class='num'>22.4%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'>0.222</td><td class='num'>12.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.330</td><td class='num'>11.3%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.503</td><td class='num'>5.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":59.32938,"lon":18.06871,"n":757,"n_cities":216,"name":"Stockholm","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0003431372549019608,"n":204,"obs":0.11274509803921569,"sig":true},{"hi":0.1,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.04076086956521739,"n":92,"obs":0.17391304347826086,"sig":true},{"hi":0.25,"lo":0.1,"mean":0.16103896103896104,"n":77,"obs":0.19480519480519481,"sig":false},{"hi":0.45,"lo":0.25,"mean":0.33053333333333335,"n":75,"obs":0.3333333333333333,"sig":false},{"hi":0.8,"lo":0.45,"mean":0.6215384615384615,"n":78,"obs":0.48717948717948717,"sig":true},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.8,"mean":0.8982666666666663,"n":75,"obs":0.7466666666666667,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.98,"mean":0.9975641025641026,"n":156,"obs":0.8269230769230769,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":1.3,"provisional":false,"rank":126,"rank_hi":161.0,"rank_lo":71.0,"reliability":0.01581388302887378,"resolution":0.08342079594803148,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"stockholm","station":"STOCKHOLM_A","timezone":"Europe/Stockholm"}